# White Widow, Free Agent: the first mode is "up to two target creatures", so a single target is as good as two. With no artifact or
# enchantment card in Bot1's graveyard only that mode can be chosen; on turn 3 Bot1 targets only Bot2's Ornithopter: it gets a
# counter, and nothing else does.

[Bot1 Deck]
White Widow, Free Agent
Ornithopter
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.White Widow, Free Agent.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.White Widow, Free Agent.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
